1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:03,150
The demo went perfectly. Every screen loaded.

2
00:00:03,150 --> 00:00:07,530
So why start a launch review with questions the demo cannot answer?

3
00:00:07,530 --> 00:00:11,730
A demo shows one person doing everything right.

4
00:00:11,730 --> 00:00:18,550
It never shows someone else's data, a retried payment, or a stale "Live".

5
00:00:18,550 --> 00:00:25,070
Each question becomes a short film.

6
00:00:25,070 --> 00:00:29,420
Flaw, control, repair, retest.

7
00:00:29,420 --> 00:00:34,160
Pay once, lose the response, retry: 2 attempts, 2 orders.

8
00:00:34,160 --> 00:00:37,470
After the repair: 2 attempts, 1 order.

9
00:00:37,470 --> 00:00:41,530
A Live label over a ten-minute-old reading.

10
00:00:41,530 --> 00:00:46,180
The label described the page, not the measurement.

11
00:00:46,180 --> 00:00:53,400
Five arcs become ten questions for any team or vendor.

12
00:00:53,400 --> 00:00:56,580
Not an audit. Not a certification.

13
00:00:56,580 --> 00:01:00,280
Synthetic fixtures. Every episode states its limits.

14
00:01:00,280 --> 00:01:04,670
Clone the fixtures. Run the tests.

15
00:01:04,670 --> 00:01:07,600
The repository, linked below.
